This report describes the design and implementation of _breakout_, a system
for processing financial tick data and identifying trading trends. We begin
with an overview of the problem and the project objectives, followed by
the system architecture and the reasoning behind the main design choices.
We then describe the implementation of the individual services and how they
work together to process data and present results to users. The evaluation
examines the correctness of the results and the system's performance under
different workloads and resource constraints, with particular attention to
throughput, latency, and scalability. Finally, we describe the contributions
of each team member and summarize the main findings of the project.
